WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:03.400
Lab 2 builds the real
thing in test instances.

2
00:00:03.400 --> 00:00:08.425
In your ServiceNow developer instance,
from Module 1, you create the three custom

3
00:00:08.425 --> 00:00:13.225
roles, one integration user and one
client-credentials integration per role.

4
00:00:13.225 --> 00:00:16.169
Then you compare each user's
roles with the call list,

5
00:00:16.169 --> 00:00:19.113
and confirm the evidence
reader can't patch a record.

6
00:00:19.113 --> 00:00:23.968
In a SailPoint sandbox tenant, you create
a reader API client and a separate

7
00:00:23.968 --> 00:00:28.275
workflow client, compare each with
the call list, and try the reader.

8
00:00:28.275 --> 00:00:32.063
How an agency gets a sandbox
is between it and SailPoint.

9
00:00:32.063 --> 00:00:37.281
Back it out before you leave: delete
the OAuth integrations, users and roles,

10
00:00:37.281 --> 00:00:39.133
and revoke any saved token;

11
00:00:39.133 --> 00:00:43.762
then delete both API clients and
anything under the output folder.

12
00:00:43.762 --> 00:00:45.980
The authors haven't run Lab 2.
